From 508f077b5af149b9084d29064b105e4bcc3b7847 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sternnick review <review@localhost>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:43:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: strip UTF-8 BOM from 9 encounter modules

A BOM is not part of Lua's grammar. Lua's own command-line loader skips a
leading BOM, but an embedded loader that hands the raw file body to
lua_load()/luaL_loadstring() can fail at 1:1 instead. If ESO's loader does
that, the nine files below never register and the require() from
bootstrap.lua:29-33 raises "module not registered" for the AS, CR, LC and
OC Factories - those four trials load dead with no visible error beyond a
chat line.

Byte-level change only: 3 bytes removed at offset 0 of each file.
Gate: tools/static_checks.py (also added by feature/ci-static-validation).

Evidence, exact line numbers and the reproduction command are in .review/code-review-2026-09-01.md (see finding F-01).
Verification: static analysis only - not run in-game.
